  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - 1. The development hereby permitted shall be commenced no later than the 15th April 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - 2. Details of facing and roofing materials shall be submitted to and approved by the local Planning Authority before building work commences.",
    "Condition : 3 - 3. Before the development commences revised details of 8 on-site carparking spaces and loading and unloading of vehicles shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the spaces shown on the approved drawing shall be laid out within the site and be available for use before the occupation of any part of the development.  Thereafter the area shall not be used for any other purpose other than the parking of cars and the loading and unloading of vehicles.",
    "Condition : 4 - 4. A schemeof landscaping shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority before the building work commences.  All planting comprised in the approved details of landscaping shall be carried out in the first planting season following the occupation of the building; and any trees or plants which within a period of 5 years from the completion of the development die, are removed or become seriously damaged or diseased, shall be replaced in the next season with others of similar size and species, uless the local planning authority gives written consent to variation.",
    "Condition : 5 - 5. The building shall not be occupied until a scheme has been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority for the retention of the brick wall along the eastern boundary of the site.  If retention proves impractical then a wall of at least 5m high shall be erected along this boundary before the building is occupied to a design and in materials to be agreed with the Local Planning Authority.\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - 6. No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am to 6:00pm Monday to Friday and 9:00am to 12:30pm and not at all on Sundays or Public holidays without prior written agreement of the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
